    "result_text": "There's exactly one test class, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes owner responses include a `displayName` field formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nTwo files touched, each with a minimal, self-contained edit:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (and getter/setter).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` computing `displayName` from the stored entity's `getLastName() + \", \" + getFirstName()`.\n\nBecause the responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and the GET responder both map through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, the field appears wherever an owner is serialized \u2014 which is what the test needs (it creates an owner, then GETs it and asserts `$.displayName` == `\"<lastName>, John\"`).\n\nStructural impact was kept low: no function bodies were grown, no new complexity added to any method \u2014 the derivation lives in a declarative mapper annotation rather than inside the pipeline function classes. `AcceptanceTest` and the full suite are green.",
